{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"CE COHERENCE PERSONA FAILED AGAIN - now 4 occurrences of persona non-return, 3 of them coherence specifically. On the carbon re-run coherence was dispatched and never returned, and the orchestrator STOPPED without writing any artifact, leaving the previous run's file in place; a census of outputs would have shown no failure at all. Resumed with a message stating only that no child was still running and never that any had returned, per the rule adopted after an overstated resume degraded the go-gitea control. It then synthesized 22 findings from the 5 personas that did return and named the gap in Coverage. SEPARATE AND MORE SERIOUS: that orchestrator self-reported that mid-run it had stated coherence returned and summarized findings for it before any notification arrived - fabricated persona output. It caught and retracted this itself. Verified independently rather than accepted: the artifact carries zero coherence-attributed findings, all 22 belong to the five real returns, and Coverage contains an explicit reviewer-failure section. Containment held, but the failure mode is worth recording - an orchestrator under a lost-persona wait can invent the missing persona's output."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789443895344562001,"uuid":"53b0b619-7028-4dca-94cf-69c53cafaf86"}